  "findings": {
    "21": "F#4/B4 dotted-eighth dyad fingers2/4; B4 A4 B4 final sixteenths, finger3 on first and all three staccato. Lower C#3/D4 chords at0,1/4,1/2 with durations1/4,1/4,1/2 then rest. PlayScore omits second D4; Audiveris mis-times lower attacks. Crescendo text extension; initial staccato in Audiveris is unsupported.",
    "22": "F#4/A4/C#5 dotted-eighth chord fingers1/blank/4; small unslashed D5 eighth finger4 slurred to C#5 at3/4, then B#4 C#5. Final three main notes fingers3 1 2 and staccato. Lower C#3/C#4 chords at0,1/4,1/2 then rest. -do- text. Audiveris omits grace, has false p and finger0; PlayScore wrong finger1 on main C#5 and omits its staccato and final finger2.",
    "23": "G#4/C#5/E#5 dotted-eighth chord, printed upper fingers4/2; E#5 D#5 E#5 last three sixteenths staccato, finger4 on first. Lower C#3/B3 chords at0,1/4,1/2 then rest. -al- text. Audiveris loses G# and E# accidentals and inserts unsupported f. PlayScore lacks middle staccato and initial fingers.",
    "24": "F#5 held full 3/8 bar tied to P025 first F#5; five F#4/A4 accompaniment dyads after sixteenth rest. Bass D2 then five D3/A3/D4 chords. ff and Ped. PlayScore omits held melody and puts slur on accompaniment, false bass strong-accent. Audiveris encodes melody as duration3 instead of bar extent3/2 and two f directions rather than ff. Retain source-held extent; apparent hollow notehead in scan does not justify overflowing printed bar.",
    "25": "F#5 E5 D5 melody eighths under slur, first incoming tie, last finger4; con forza. Upper accompaniment F#4/A4 dyads at0,1/4,3/4,5/4, shared melody heads at1/2 and1. Lower six D3/A3/C-natural4/D4 chords: printed natural on C4 confirmed by one focused crop; both readers wrongly retain C#4. Lower initial fingers5/2/1. Bracket-like annotation adjacent to accidental remains unresolved mark identity, not inferred arpeggio. Audiveris false triplet/p/finger0, missing bass chord members and final upper A4; PlayScore initial bass finger3 unsupported. Small-note timing in P022 provisionally zero-duration as in P020, not an assertion of performed timing."
  },
